name: sim.getVisionSensorDepth
description: Reads the depth buffer of a vision sensor. The returned data doesn't make sense if sim.handleVisionSensor wasn't called previously
luaSynopsis: bytes depth = sim.getVisionSensorDepth(int sensorHandle, int options = 0, list pos = [0, 0], list size = [0, 0])
pythonSynopsis: buffer depth, int[2] resolution = sim.getVisionSensorDepth(int sensorHandle, int options = 0, int[2] pos = {0, 0}, int[2] size = {0, 0})
inputs:
1. sensorHandle: handle of the vision sensor
2. options: options, bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): the returned values indicate distances in meters, otherwise return values are in the range of 0.0 - 1.0 (0.0 = closest to sensor (i.e. close clipping plane), 1.0 = farthest from sensor (i.e. far clipping plane))
3. pos: position of the depth buffer portion to retrieve. Defaults to [0 0]
4. size: size of the depth buffer portion to retrieve. Defaults to [0 0], which corresponds to [resolutionX resolutionY]
outputs:
1. depth: the depth buffer. Use sim.unpackFloatTable to obtain an array of values
2. resolution: the vision sensor resolution
replacedBy:
- name: getDepth, class: visionSensor, file: visionSensor_getDepth.method
- name: depth, class: visionSensor, file: visionSensor_depth.property
- name: packedDepth, class: visionSensor, file: visionSensor_packedDepth.property
